---
import MainLayout from '../../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
const lastUpdated = "August 2026";
---

<MainLayout
  title="Editorial Guidelines"
  description="How Pixelquil researches, writes, and maintains accurate content across every tool page."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-20">
    <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full bg-brand-50 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-brand-600">
      Editorial Guidelines
    </span>
    <h1 class="mt-6 text-4xl font-bold text-slate-900 sm:text-5xl">How we write and maintain content</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-500">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <div class="mt-10 space-y-8 text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">Written from real usage</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Every tool page's written content is grounded in actual production experience, not
          written speculatively. Technical explanations, like why a missing SVG viewBox breaks
          scaling, or how the SVG specification permits embedded scripts, are checked against
          primary sources such as the official SVG and schema.org specifications rather than
          repeated secondhand from other sites.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">Accuracy standards</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Where content references a technical standard, security mechanism, or specification, we
          aim to cite the actual behavior correctly rather than a simplified or exaggerated
          version of it. Where a tool has a genuine limitation, that limitation is stated directly
          rather than glossed over, for example, noting that automatically generated color scales
          are a practical approximation, not a perceptually precise model.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">Updates and corrections</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Tool pages are revisited and updated as tools themselves evolve or as errors are found.
          If you spot something inaccurate or outdated, we welcome corrections through the
          <a href="/contact/" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline">contact page</a>, and take
          them seriously.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">No paid placement</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Tool recommendations, comparisons, and technical explanations on this site are not
          influenced by paid placement. Where advertising appears on the site, it is served
          through Google AdSense and clearly separated from editorial content.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</MainLayout>